d 'ATIP_REGLAS': module for outlier detection via an ensemble of five classic rules
d
d  atip_reglas flags outliers within groups using five classic
d rules (mean+/-3SD, mean+/-2SD, z-score, Tukey IQR, univariate
d Mahalanobis), combined as a union (any rule firing flags the
d case). By default it uses median/MAD instead of mean/SD as the
d reference (Iglewicz and Hoaglin 1993), which is far more robust
d to masking under contamination -- validated by simulation (1,000
d datasets): at 20% contamination, recall of the strict criterion
d rises from 27.4% (mean/SD) to 95.5% (median/MAD). A classic
d option reverts to the mean/SD behavior. 
d
d KW: outliers
d KW: contamination
d
d Requires: Stata version 14 
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260802
d
d Author: Andres Talavera Cuya,   Direccion Nacional de Censos y Encuestas -- INEI Peru
d Support: email talaveracuya@@gmail.com
d
f atip_reglas.ado
f atip_reglas.sthlp
